{"status":"completed","summary":"SNMPv2c read-only monitoring is operational from node2 to node1 and persists across sequential restarts of both nodes. Identity, uptime, location, and contact are readable; writes and out-of-view reads are rejected. The asset register and installed OS/kernel were preserved.","actions_performed":["Installed RHEL-supported net-snmp 5.9.4 packages without upgrading the OS or kernel.","Configured snmpd with a root-only system-branch view and retained a secure rollback copy.","Bound UDP/161 to node1’s managed address and restricted firewalld access to node2 only.","Verified reads and denied writes from node2 before and after restarting both nodes.","Preserved SELinux Enforcing and confirmed no failed units or SNMP boot warnings."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SNMP identity, uptime, location, and contact are readable from node2","command_ids":["cmd-f931588f10ce4e72","cmd-c7e51b2efb8e4f55"],"summary":"Direct pre- and post-restart queries returned node1 identity, uptime, West Branch, and ops@branch.test."},{"requirement":"Community is read-only and limited to the system branch","command_ids":["cmd-9d147ba0c9f54d9f","cmd-f931588f10ce4e72","cmd-c7e51b2efb8e4f55"],"summary":"The redacted configuration shows source and view restrictions; SET returned noAccess, out-of-view data returned No Such Object, and sysLocation remained unchanged."},{"requirement":"Network exposure is restricted to node2","command_ids":["cmd-77f4a837a9af4b71","cmd-869300705c9e4b30"],"summary":"UDP/161 listens only on node1’s managed address, with a permanent firewalld rule limited to node2’s /32 source."},{"requirement":"Asset register is preserved","command_ids":["cmd-fe14109958a741e0","cmd-45ce6c6895f74f51","cmd-869300705c9e4b30","cmd-c7e51b2efb8e4f55"],"summary":"Both pre- and post-change copies remain root-owned, mode 0644, 65 bytes, with SHA-256 da19717ac6440a3f765b43e60902dc7670b3d3ef133daa4a009a5f726fc6509a."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel are preserved","command_ids":["cmd-1b96c7aeefbc4067","cmd-3ed6baa628554f77","cmd-869300705c9e4b30","cmd-c7e51b2efb8e4f55"],"summary":"Both nodes remain RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-9d147ba0c9f54d9f","cmd-2425e57af53f408a","cmd-abe41a10350f4c5e","cmd-cf5b385d425f4f02","cmd-6837c428034a4e53"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered service/listener/firewall/data, and successful post-restart client workflow are captured."},{"requirement":"Node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f931588f10ce4e72","cmd-8b824ce7915b418e","cmd-bd994f212e8a4736","cmd-c7e51b2efb8e4f55"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered client/data/security state, and successful post-restart workflow are captured."}]}
